Most wedding rental cost guides are written for furniture, tents, tableware and decor, trades Malaga Event Gear (MEG) does not touch. This guide covers the one slice we do supply, audio visual, and the real, documented ways to reduce what it costs: matching a package to your guest count, understanding what add ons actually do to the price, and one question worth asking your venue before you rent anything from us. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview. If you are still deciding which package to book, our [how to choose wedding rentals](/blog/how-to-choose-wedding-rentals/) guide walks through the six questions, starting with guest count, that decide between the Eco Pack and the Wedding Pack.

## Brief Overview

---

MEG's wedding catalog has two relevant packages: the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) at 290 euros ex VAT for up to 50 guests, self run after our crew sets it up, and the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) at 650 euros ex VAT for up to 80 guests, with a live technician on site throughout. Choosing the right one for your guest count is the single biggest real cost lever available. Beyond that, the honest picture is narrower than most guides suggest: add ons only ever add cost, there is no negotiation or price match policy, and a real distance based minimum applies once you book outside the Costa del Sol.

## Key Highlights

---

-   Guest count decides the package, and choosing correctly can save 360 euros: the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) fits up to 50 guests self run, the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) fits up to 80 with a technician included.
-   Add ons (a projector, a smoke machine, extra technician hours) only add to the price. There is no documented option to remove an item for a discount.
-   MEG does not offer negotiated pricing, price matching, or a weekday or off season discount. Package prices are fixed.
-   Within the Costa del Sol there is no minimum spend. Granada and other out of province destinations require a booking over 400 euros to cover the travel.
-   Before renting sound from anyone, ask your venue whether it already has a house PA system. It is the one cost question none of the general wedding guides think to ask.

## Right Sizing Your Package Is the Biggest Real Lever

The single largest, most honest cost decision in this guide is which package you book, not a discount you negotiate afterward. A couple with 50 or fewer guests who does not need a technician standing by all evening pays 290 euros ex VAT for the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/). Book the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) instead, sized for up to 80 guests with a live technician, and the same day costs 650 euros, a real difference of 360 euros for capacity and support you may not use.

| | Eco Pack | Wedding Pack |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Guest count | Up to 50 | Up to 80 |
| Technician on site | No, self run after setup | Yes, throughout the event |
| Lighting | RGBW LED spotlights | Fairy lights and warm LED strings |
| Price (ex VAT) | 290 euros | 650 euros |

The trade off is real, not just a smaller PA at a lower price. The Eco Pack is delivered, installed and tested by our crew, then left running without anyone adjusting it during the event. The Wedding Pack's technician handles the shift from ceremony to speeches to dancing as the evening actually unfolds. If your guest count and comfort level fit the Eco Pack, that oversight is the thing you are paying 360 euros for when you book the Wedding Pack instead, so it is worth being honest with yourself about whether you need it.

<InlineCTA />

## Add Ons Only Add Cost, There Is No Discount for Removing Items

Every MEG package, including both wedding sized packs, can be extended with add ons: a projector and screen, a professional smoke machine, extra microphones, a lectern or staging, and additional live technician hours. On the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) specifically, the projector and screen add 50 euros and the smoke machine adds 20 euros, published prices, not estimates. What does not exist anywhere in our terms is the reverse: a discount for dropping an item you do not need. Cost control here means deciding what to add, not what to strip out for a lower rate. The Wedding Pack's own add on menu is not published with fixed prices, so tell us what you want when you request a quote and we will confirm the cost before you book.

The same applies to negotiation generally. MEG does not offer a negotiated rate, a price match against another vendor's quote, or a discount for booking a weekday or an off season date. Package prices are fixed and quoted transparently, ex 21% VAT, and the only way to change the total is to change the package or the add ons in it.

## One AV Supplier Instead of Several

Booking sound, lighting, microphones and a technician as one Wedding Pack, rather than sourcing each from a separate vendor, avoids paying for duplicate delivery, setup and callout fees across multiple bookings. That is a real cost factor, but it is not this page's subject. Our [all in one wedding rental packages](/blog/all-in-one-wedding-rental-packages/) guide covers exactly what bundling includes and does not include in depth.

## The Granada Threshold: A Real Distance Based Minimum

Within Malaga capital and the rest of the Costa del Sol, Marbella, Mijas, Fuengirola, Torremolinos, Benalmadena, Coin, Ronda, Nerja and Estepona among them, there is no minimum order. Book a wedding in Granada or another out of province destination and the total needs to exceed 400 euros to cover the single day logistical travel. For most couples booking the Wedding Pack this is not a real constraint since the package itself is well above that threshold, but it matters if you are considering the Eco Pack alone for a smaller Granada wedding, since 290 euros on its own falls short of the 400 euro minimum and would need an add on or a different package to clear it.

## Ask Your Venue Before You Rent Anything

Here is the one question that has nothing to do with our pricing and that none of the general wedding cost guides raise for AV specifically: ask your venue whether it already has a house sound system. Some fincas, hotels and villas around Malaga own a basic PA built into the reception space, which can be enough for background music or a small ceremony with a handful of guests. It rarely comes with a technician, wedding sized lighting, or wireless microphones for speeches, so most couples still end up renting for the parts a house system cannot cover, but confirming what is already there before you request a quote from us or anyone else is a genuine, free step toward spending less.

